@prefix gmeow:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix prov:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix snomed: <http://snomed.info/id/> .

# Term equivalences for the awareness slice — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-awareness.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.
# All alignments are BY REFERENCE (Principle 5); GMEOW never imports an external axiom.

gmeow:mapsetAwareness a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    rdfs:label "awareness mapping set"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The SSSOM mapping set for the awareness slice — aligns the awareness modes and arousal levels to external sleep/wake, consciousness, and provenance vocabularies."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/awareness> ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-awareness.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/awareness" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment """Awareness slice alignments — the state-of-the-experiencer axis: human awareness modes and arousal levels beside the machine operational modes (the Principle-5 bridge).

        EXTERNAL FRAMEWORKS NAMED IN PROSE (no stable, freely-resolvable RDF namespace is imported; GMEOW imports no external axiom, Principle 5):
        * NSWO (Non-REM/REM Sleep–Wake Ontology) and sleep-staging vocabularies: the
          clinical account of wake / REM / non-REM stages is the conceptual basis of the
          sleep-related awareness modes (gmeow:modeAsleep / gmeow:modeREM / gmeow:modeDreaming).
        * SNOMED CT consciousness concepts: the clinical consciousness-state terms
          (alert, drowsy, obtunded, stuporous, comatose) parallel the awareness levels and
          the low-arousal modes; SNOMED CT is a licensed terminology, named in prose only.
        * Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS): the clinical arousal scale to which the lowest rungs
          gmeow:levelObtunded and gmeow:levelUnresponsive correspond by reference — an ordinal
          arousal mapping, not an imported numeric scale.
        * W3C PROV-O: the AI operational regimes (gmeow:modeOnlineInference / gmeow:modeTraining /
          gmeow:modeSampling) are also describable as prov:Activity instances; the overlap is
          recorded as a deliberately low-confidence relatedMatch, not a closeMatch.

        The machine awareness modes are SIBLINGS of the human modes bridged by ANALOGY, NOT by
        equivalence (Principle 5): no owl:sameAs / owl:equivalentClass couples a machine mode to a
        human one, and the analogue pairings (online-inference≈waking, offline-replay≈dreaming) are
        documented in prose, never asserted.""" ;
    gmeow:setTrailer "# No frame-selecting mapping (Principle 9): GMEOW asserts no single 'correct' theory of consciousness or sleep staging; the value-vocab members are co-equal, and the human↔machine analogue is by reference only." .

# Sleep state — gmeow:modeAsleep names the general sleep state. Clinical terminologies model
# being asleep as a finding; gmeow:modeAsleep is a state-of-the-experiencer awareness value. The
# shared notion is the sleep state, hence a deliberately low-confidence relatedMatch (not
# closeMatch). The object is the SNOMED CT "Asleep" finding; the NSWO / sleep-staging account
# named in the set comment is the wider conceptual basis, by reference (Principle 5).
gmeow:modeAsleep skos:relatedMatch snomed:248218005 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-awareness.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.3 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:modeAsleep is a state-of-the-experiencer awareness value; SNOMED CT 'Asleep' (248218005) is a clinical finding. Shared notion: the sleep state — loose relatedMatch only; the NSWO sleep-staging account is referenced in the set comment, not imported."
|} .

# Glasgow Coma Scale — gmeow:levelUnresponsive is the arousal floor of coma. The GCS is an
# ordinal clinical arousal scale; gmeow:levelUnresponsive corresponds to its lowest range by
# reference. The shared notion is unarousable unresponsiveness, hence a low-confidence relatedMatch.
gmeow:levelUnresponsive skos:relatedMatch snomed:371632003 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-awareness.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.3 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:levelUnresponsive is the arousal floor; the object is a coma / Glasgow-Coma-Scale consciousness concept named by reference (SNOMED CT 'Coma'). Shared notion: unarousable unresponsiveness — loose relatedMatch only, no imported numeric scale."
|} .

# PROV-O 'Activity' — gmeow:modeOnlineInference is a machine operational state, also describable
# as a prov:Activity (a serving run). PROV models the ACTIVITY by which entities are used and
# generated; gmeow:modeOnlineInference is a state-of-the-experiencer awareness value. The overlap
# is the running-process notion, hence a deliberately low-confidence relatedMatch.
gmeow:modeOnlineInference skos:relatedMatch prov:Activity {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-awareness.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.4 ;
    gmeow:comment "gmeow:modeOnlineInference is a state-of-the-experiencer awareness value; prov:Activity is a provenance process type. Shared notion: a running operational process — loose relatedMatch only, the awareness mode is not asserted to BE a prov:Activity."
|} .
